Something I was thinking of adding was a new monster (human actualy), Assassin.
They would usualy leave you alone and would be very formidable foes.  But, each
would have a scroll (or two) in their possesion.  These scrolls would be of a
new type, "a contract", that would have the name of a particular person (NPC)
in the dungeon.  If that NPC is killed AND the bearer of the contract escapes
the dungeon THEN they are rewarded with a large (possibly stated in the
contract) sum of money (or points).

I suppose you could have Chaotic Assassins, Lawful Bounty Hunters, and Neutral
Executioners (it's just my job!) so some would be friendly and other would not.

What do people think?

